Trace the response-policy round trip under WEBKIT_SOUP_LOG.

Patch 0007 settled where the https hang is NOT: with its read-loop tracing in
the running image, an https load prints no [read] lines at all, so
NetworkDataTaskSoup::read() is never called.  The 512 bytes in the soup wire
log are libsoup's own MIME-sniff read, made inside soup_session_send_async()
before WebKit ever touches the stream -- not the browser consuming the body.

read() is reached only from the completion handler of didReceiveResponse(),
and for a main resource that completion is an IPC round trip:

  network   NetworkResourceLoader::didReceiveResponse
              -> WebResourceLoader::DidReceiveResponse            (IPC ->)
  web       WebResourceLoader::didReceiveResponse
              -> policy decided (via the UI process)
              -> NetworkResourceLoader::ContinueDidReceiveResponse (IPC <-)
  network   continueDidReceiveResponse -> completion(Use) -> read()

http completes this loop and https never does.  The release logs that cover
every hop (LOADER_RELEASE_LOG, WEBRESOURCELOADER_RELEASE_LOG) are compiled out
of this build -- WEBKIT_DEBUG=Network prints nothing -- so the stalled hop is
invisible.  This puts one line at each hop, in both processes, gated on
WEBKIT_SOUP_LOG like 0006/0007.  The last [hop] line printed names the hop
that never happened.

Upstream: not reportable -- bring-up instrumentation.

--- a/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/soup/NetworkDataTaskSoup.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/soup/NetworkDataTaskSoup.cpp
@@ -375,6 +375,11 @@
 
     GUniqueOutPtr<GError> error;
     GRefPtr<GInputStream> inputStream = adoptGRef(soup_session_send_finish(soupSession, result, &error.outPtr()));
+    // Round-trip tracing, on with WEBKIT_SOUP_LOG (see 0008): soup has finished
+    // its part -- headers parsed, MIME type sniffed -- and hands over the body
+    // stream here.  Everything after this line until read() is policy IPC.
+    if (getenv("WEBKIT_SOUP_LOG"))
+        WTFLogAlways("[hop] net: soup stream ready (%s)", error ? error->message : "ok");
     if (error)
         task->didFail(ResourceError::httpError(data->soupMessage.get(), error.get()));
     else
@@ -412,6 +417,9 @@
     m_response.setDeprecatedNetworkLoadMetrics(Box<NetworkLoadMetrics>::create(m_networkLoadMetrics));
 
     didReceiveResponse(ResourceResponse(m_response), NegotiatedLegacyTLS::No, PrivateRelayed::No, std::nullopt, [this, protectedThis = Ref { *this }](PolicyAction policyAction) {
+        // The far end of the round trip: only from here can read() start.
+        if (getenv("WEBKIT_SOUP_LOG"))
+            WTFLogAlways("[hop] net: policy completion arrived, action=%d state=%d", (int)policyAction, (int)m_state);
         if (m_state == State::Canceling || m_state == State::Completed) {
